SIMPLE  =                    T / Standard FITS format                           BITPIX  =                    8 / 8 bits ASCII                                   NAXIS   =                    0 / No image data                                  END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             XTENSION= 'BINTABLE'           / Table extension                                BITPIX  =                    8 / Binary data                                    NAXIS   =                    2 / Two dimensional table data                     NAXIS1  =                   20 / Bytes per row                                  NAXIS2  =                  246 / Number of rows in the table                    PCOUNT  =                    0 / The heap size in bytes after data matrix       GCOUNT  =                    1 / Only one group                                 TFIELDS =                    5 / Number of columns in the table                 TFORM1  = '1E'                 / The data type of this column                   TTYPE1  = 'radius'             / The radial coordinate on the accretion disc    TUNIT1  = 'rg'                 / Gravitational radii rg = GM/c^2                TFORM2  = '1E'                 / The data type of this column                   TTYPE2  = 'em'                 / The emissivity value itself                    TUNIT2  = 'arbitrary'          / The unit of this column                        TFORM3  = '1E'                 / The data type of this column                   TTYPE3  = 'time'               / Corona-to-disc light-travel time               TUNIT3  = 'tg'                 / Light-crossing time tg = GM/c^3                TFORM4  = '1E'                 / The data type of this column                   TTYPE4  = 'energyshift'        / Corona-to-disc energyshift                     TFORM5  = '1E'                 / The data type of this column                   TTYPE5  = 'local_theta'        / The incident angle off disc surface normal.    TUNIT5  = 'rad'                / The unit of this column                        EXTNAME = 'EMISSIVITY'         / This is an axisymmetric emissivity table       KZVERSN = '0.3.4-3efc15c9'     / kerrz version                                  KZMODEL = 'LAMPPOST'           / This is a kerrz lamppost corona table          LPHEIGHT=              5.00000 / Lamppost height in rg                          LPRVEL  =              0.00000 / Lamppost radial velocity in units of c         LPGAMMA =              2.00000 / Lamppost powerlaw photon index                 PF_BH   =              0.18200 / Photon fraction event horizon                  PF_INF  =              0.32600 / Photon fraction infinity                       PF_NONE =              0.00000 / Photon fraction with unknown status            PF_DISC =              0.49200 / Photon fraction accretion disc                 PF_AISCO=              0.48000 / Photon fraction above the ISCO                 PF_BISCO=              0.01200 / Photon fraction below the ISCO                 MASS    =              1.00000 / The mass scale of the black hole               SPIN    =              0.99800 / The dimensionless spin of black hole           END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             